From 2fdf7961dd6566606488d9cbadd0bfb7964027f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Creitin Gameplays <clton999@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 01:39:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] mali: adapt qogirl6 platform glue to the r28p0 DDK and
 this board

Rewrite the Unisoc qogirl6 platform integration so the built-in driver
works with the imported r28p0-01eac0 core and the Moto E32 (hawaii,
UMS9230/T606) boot device tree:

- the board uses generic "syscons"/"syscon-names" properties; the
  top-force-shutdown power switch is resolved by name through
  syscon_regmap_lookup_by_name/syscon_get_args_by_name (both exported by
  this kernel) instead of the vendor trees phandle-with-args properties
- the gpu_top_state and power-domain state syscons of the vendor trees
  are not present here; the health waits degrade to a short settle delay
- the DDK platform mechanism builds the glue into the composite module
  (mali_kbase-y += platform/qogirl6/... ) instead of obj-y, which never
  resolved to an object under in-tree kbuild
- vendor changes on top of the DDK are added to the core of_match table
  (sprd,mali-natt), so the stock GPU node binds without DT surgery
- the DVFS stays in the platform glue: boot frequency from
  "sprd,dvfs-default" (the DT entry), T606 GPLL trimmed to 650 MHz,
  core voltage index maps per speed bin, QoS programming; MALI_DEVFREQ
  is off, matching the vendor behavior on this device where devfreq runs
  pinned to 650 MHz anyway
- removed r40p0-only frequency statistics hooks (kbase_pm_statistics_*)
  and struct kbase_device fields absent from r28p0
- guard all clock handles and the nvmem speed-bin read

Builds clean with clang 11 under arch=arm64; the driver is built-in
(CONFIG_MALI_MIDGARD=y, CONFIG_MALI_PLATFORM_NAME="qogirl6").
